  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 accuracy. The key open question is whether adding the image modality can improve upon this strong RNA-only baseline. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), suggesting limited standalone value, but it may still provide complementary signal in a fused setting. Config_032 directly extends config_006 by adding resnet50 image features with the same transformer aggregation and a simple concat fusion, isolating the effect of multimodal fusion on top of the best-known RNA configuration. This is the cleanest single-variable extension of our best result. If it fails to beat 0.653, we can confidently conclude RNA-only multiprofile is optimal and use remaining budget to confirm; if it helps, we can explore weighted fusion or ViT-L in the remaining 3 experiments."
}

